\ldblquote Do you really have to throw it away like that?\rdblquote  Riette asked. \ldblquote You loved that thing?\par
Claudine glanced up at him with a look that showed she had no intention of changing her mind. Sh e then casually tossed the bracelet she was holding into the fire that was blazing in the fireplace. The torn-up letter followed close behind.\par
\ldblquote As far as I\rquote m concerned, anything that she has touched is defiled?\rdblquote  she said.\par
Riette doubted his ears for a moment. He couldn\rquote t believe that she was talking about her fiance\rquote s mistress in the casual tone of voice one would use to comment on the weather.\par
Putting his hand to his aching forehead, he stood up and walked towards the fireplace. Claudine watched as the fire devoured the items that had been tainted by Layla\rquote s touch.\par
When Claudine\rquote s maid had brought in a small package for her, Riette had paid it little mind.\par
Claudine was the most envied lady in Karlsbar\rquote s high society, and she was constantly receiving letters and gifts from ladies who wanted to curry favor with her. He was taken aback, however, when he had learned that the package was from Layla Llewellyn. Especially once he saw what was inside.\par
\par
The broken bracelet that Claudine had dropped on the ground in the garden had been repaired. It looked good as new. Apparently Layla had paid for this out of her own pocket. She had also included a letter, in which she had apologized, and had confirmed that her relationship with Matthias was exactly as Claudine had guessed it to be.\par
Riette had already assumed this to be the case, so it hadn\rquote t surprised him. Instead, what had shocked him was the reaction of Claudine, his beloved cousin.\par
She had proceeded to tell him with casual indifference about all the things she had done to Layla \f1\emdash how she had gotten Kyle Ettman to confront her about her relationship with the duke, and how when that didn\rquote t work, she had met with her herself and acted cruelly towards her in order to scare her from doing anything more. These cold, underhanded tricks seemed unbefitting of the dignified Claudine he knew.\par
\ldblquote Isn\rquote t this something that you could talk over with Matthias?\rdblquote  he asked. \ldblquote Duke Herhardt doesn\rquote t know about it. And he must never find out about\par
it.\rdblquote  She sauntered back to where she had been sitting and sat down again. \lquote Do you think that\rquote s cowardly of me?\rdblquote  she asked, grinning at Riette. \ldblquote Sure, rather than messing with my unassailable fiance. I\rquote m focusing my efforts on his mistress. Is that just? Maybe not. But so what? Picking on a lowly opponent may be cowardly, but it\rquote s not especially unfair, is it?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote What?\rdblquote  he asked.\par
\ldblquote Once Layla is gone, everything else will go back to the way it was. There\rquote s no need to confront Duke Herhardt and risk causing bigger problems.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote If Layla goes away, do you really expect that the powerful Duke Herhardt won\rquote t be able to find her again?\rdblquote  he asked, sighing.\par
\par
In the letter Layla had sent to Claudine, she had said that she would be leaving Matthias before the day of the wedding, and had begged Claudine to keep it a secret from him until then. She had said she was sorry for the unpardonable wrongs she had committed, and that even though she knew she could never make up for it, she was disappearing from their lives as a way of seeking atonement.\par
To Riette\rquote s surprise, the letter made it seem like Layla wasn\rquote t going to miss Matthias at all. Rather, she seemed desperate to get away from him by whatever means necessary. He knew, however, that if the affair had begun out of Matthias\rquote s lust and obsession, then Layla wouldn\rquote t be able to end it simply by leaving.\par
\ldblquote After he and I get married,\rdblquote  Claudine said, \ldblquote all I have to do is bear him a son who will be his heir. Other than that. I don\rquote t particularly want much to do with him\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Is that all the meaning that there is to your life? Just to become duchess and give birth lo the next Duke Herhardt? Once you\rquote ve completed that task, is your life over?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote It\rquote s not the only meaning\'85 I\rquote d say it\rquote s probably about half. But I never want to witness Duke Herhardt enamored with that lowly girl again.\rdblquote  Her eyes slowly narrowed. \ldblquote I\rquote d rather that she die. If she vanished from this world forever, my fiance would never again be reduced to the vulgar, disgusting man he becomes in her presence. He would be a perfect gentleman for the rest of his life-just what I want.\par
\ldblquote Claudine!\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote I\rquote m serious, Riette. Every day, I kill that girl in my mind. I realize that the whole thing is Matthias\rquote s fault, not hers, but what can I do? He has to become\par
\par
my husband. It would be dreadfully inconvenient if he were to die on me,\rdblquote  she said, sneering.\par
Riette\rquote s eyes sunk with concern as he watched her. Duke Herhardt was the key to Claudine living the life she had always wanted for herself, so he couldn\rquote t step between them. However, he could plainly see that she was no longer acting like herself.\par
He felt indignant. Why does he get you instead of me? Why does that man who makes you act like someone else, who doesn\rquote t even love you, get to have you? He stood up. \ldblquote As prestigious as the title of duchess may be, it\rquote s not worth destroying yourself for, Claudine.\rdblquote  He started slowly walking towards her. \ldblquote You should break off your engagement.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote What\'85?\rdblquote  she replied, taken aback.\par
\ldblquote Don\rquote t sell your soul for the promise of honor,\rdblquote  he said, getting down on one knee in front of her.\par
She looked closely at his face to try to tell if he was joking, but he looked dead serious.\par
He had told her that she should leave Matthias and marry him countless times before, but had always acted like it was no more than a joke. Thus she had always laughed it off. It was an unwritten rule between the two of them that he would only ever make such pronouncements in jest. But now he was blatantly breaking the rule.\par
\ldblquote If I break off my engagement with the duke, do you really think that you and I could just get married instead?\rdblquote  she asked derisively.\par
However, his will remained firm. \ldblquote Nothing\rquote s impossible, Claudine\ldblquote\par
\ldblquote Get a grip, Marquess Lindman. Think of what people will say! \lquote Lady Claudine Brandt tried out one of her cousins before changing her mind and marrying the other.\rquote  \lquote Marquess Lindman betrayed his best friend by stealing\par
\par
his fiancee.\rquote  Don\rquote t you see? Our reputations would be dragged through the mud, when it\rquote s Matthias and Layla who are the disgraceful ones\rquote\rdblquote\par
He let out a long sigh and took her by the hand. \ldblquote I don\rquote t care.\ldblquote\par
\ldblquote My family would never accept it,\rdblquote  she said. \ldblquote Neither would yours.\rdblquote  \ldblquote I know.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote If we chose to be together, we would be all but banished from the world. Do you really love me enough for it to be worth that?\rdblquote  Thick tears started to fall from her bloodshot eyes.\par
A faint grin appeared on his lips as he nodded. \ldblquote Yes, I do.\rdblquote  He gently squeezed her hands. \ldblquote I love you, Claudine. So please, marry me, and we can run away together.\rdblquote\par
