After she finished grading her students\rquote  quizzes, Layla rubbed her stiff shoulders and stood up from her bedroom desk.\par
It was already well past nine o\rquote clock. Earlier in the evening, Phoebe had returned to the cottage without a note. Fortunately, it seemed that the duke would not be summoning her tonight.\par
Letting out a long sigh of relief, she opened the door off her closet. Just then, there was a tapping sound at her window. She knew that Phoebe was inside her cage. She had checked that the door was securely locked several times.\par
As she was wondering if she had imagined it, she heard more tapping, louder than the first time. It definitely wasn\rquote t Phoebe. There was no way that pigeon\rquote s tiny beak could make such a loud sound. What could be causing the sound, then\'85?\par
Half in doubt, she opened the curtains. She was relieved not to seethe duke there, but her suspicion only increased. If it wasn\rquote t him, who could it have been?\par
After gazing at the darkness outside the window for a moment, she cautiously opened it. Just as she was about to conclude that she had just been hearing things, she noticed a long shadow on the ground outside the window.\par
She followed the shadow with her eyes until she let out a yelp when saw its source. \ldblquote Ah\'85!\rdblquote  If she hadn\rquote t quickly put her hands over her mouth, she might have screamed loudly enough to wake Uncle Bill.\par
\par
\ldblquote Good evening, Layla.\rdblquote  the duke said, chuckling quietly as he leaned languidly against the wall next to the window.\par
\ldblquote Wh-what are you doing here, Your Grace?\rdblquote  \ldblquote Good question. Why do you think?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Go away! Right now!\rdblquote  She looked uneasily back and forth between the closed door of her room and the man standing outside the window. Uncle Bill was usually asleep by this hour, but that didn\rquote t bring her much relief. \ldblquote Please hurry up and leave. I hate it when you-\rdblquote\par
Before she could finish, he shut her up by putting his lips to hers. He proceeded to give her a long, slow kiss as he firmly held her face against his. She felt even more anxious as she heard him starting to laugh.\par
Finally letting her go, he said, \ldblquote Come outside.\rdblquote\par
Her brow slowly furrowed as she stared at his wet lips. \ldblquote No!\rdblquote  \ldblquote Then I\rquote ll come inside.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Why are you doing this?\rdblquote  she asked, reaching out to grab his arm in order to stop him from walking around to the cottage\rquote s front door. \ldblquote Please, just go! I can\rquote t leave home right now.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Why not?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Uncle Bill might still be awake.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote So what?\rdblquote  He glanced at her face, then at the windowsill, then at her face again.\par
When she understood what he was getting at, she sighed in frustration. \ldblquote You want me to climb out the window? Right now? Why should I?\rdblquote  \ldblquote Because I want you to,\rdblquote  he replied, flashing a warm but arrogant smile at\par
her.\par
She pulled down her sleeves and rubbed the saliva from her lips. She knew\par
\par
that this wild man was not going to give up. Causing a ruckus would only\par
\par
make things more dangerous for her.\par
After glaring at him, she hurriedly locked the door to her room and returned to the window. \ldblquote It\rquote s not very gentlemanly of you to ask a lady to climb out a window.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote I wouldn\rquote t expect such a reproach to come from a lady who\rquote s as good at climbing trees as you.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote I haven\rquote t climbed trees in a long time!\rdblquote  With that, she deftly climbed up onto the windowsill.\par
He approached the window to help her down, but she didn\rquote t need any help.\par
She nimbly climbed down in an instant.\par
\ldblquote Seems like you haven\rquote t lost the hang of it,\rdblquote  he muttered, chuckling. He then closed the window and grabbed her hand.\par
The two of them passed through the backyard towards the forest path. Once they had gone far enough to be out of sight of the cottage, she breathed a sigh of relief.\par
After a moment, she realized that they weren\rquote t on the path that led to his cabin. \ldblquote Um\'85 we\rquote re going the wrong way, aren\rquote t we?\rdblquote  she asked.\par
\ldblquote This is the way,\rdblquote  he casually replied. He was taking her in a completely different direction.\par
The moonlight peeking through the branches shone on their hands as he Intertwined his fingers with hers.\par
\ldblquote I have something to show you,\rdblquote  he whispered. His voice was as soft and gentle as the early- spring night.\par
