Easy, Ever So Easy.\par
\par
\par
Layla showed up early at the duke\rquote s dark, quiet cabin. She retrieved the key from the pocket of her cardigan and opened the door. As always, she left\par
the lights off. By now, she was so familiar with the interior of the cabin, she had no problem getting around in the darkness. She would likely still remember the floor plan long after departing from Arvis.\par
She calmly surveyed the drawing room. It reminded her of the beautiful birdcage that housed the duke\rquote s canary. She sat on the sofa and stared at her feet for a moment then impulsively stood up again and went out onto the balcony. There was a cool, gentle breeze blowing in from the river. The cold, winter night when she and the duke had agreed on their deal, the deal that would determine Uncle Bill\rquote s fate, now seemed like the distant past. It was hard to believe that it was just a season ago.\par
She slowly approached the balcony\rquote s railing and looked down at the Schulter River. Having been frozen over throughout the winter, the river was now flowing freely. The bright moonlight was glittering on the surface of the water.\par
\par
\ldblquote So pretty\'85\rdblquote  she muttered, thinking, I hope my heart will soon be able to flow as freely as this river.\par
She was roused from her thoughts by the sound of the duke approaching. She flinched, then looked up and saw him leaning against the railing near her. As they made eye contact, the look in his eyes was as cool and gentle as the night breeze.\par
\ldblquote The flowers are in bloom,\rdblquote  he said, breaking the silence.\par
Her eyes widened at the unexpected remark. \ldblquote The flowers? Oh\'85\rdblquote  She looked away awkwardly and tightened her grip on the railing as she recalled the promise she had made him.\par
\ldblquote Next weekend should be perfect,\rquote  he added. \ldblquote Pardon?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote For us to go to the place that you said you\rquote d show me.\rdblquote  He slowly reached out and caressed her blonde hair, which was being gently tossed about by the breeze.\par
She stared at him, not sure what to say. He was dressed more casually than usual, wearing a cream-colored tennis sweater and flannel pants. She almost felt like she was looking at a stranger.\par
\ldblquote Instead of next weekend, how about this weekend?\rdblquote  she asked, forcing herself to smile. \ldblquote All the flowers are pretty much in bloom already, after all.\rdblquote  I can\rquote t let myself lose strength now, she thought. Not after working so hard to get to this point.\par
\ldblquote I have to go to Ratse this weekend,\rdblquote  he replied, sweeping his hair away from his face\par
Usually he kept his hair slicked back with pomade, but now it appeared not to have any product in it. His bangs sat freely on his forehead. Seeing him like this, the image of him as a schoolchild suddenly flashed into her mind. Then\par
\par
she remembered when she was a young girl wandering around the heavenly Arvis, when she had run into him, Arvis\rquote s lord, without knowing who he was at first.\par
\ldblquote You\rquote re going to Ratse?\rdblquote  she asked.\par
\ldblquote Yes, for the empress\rquote s birthday party. I also have some work to do while I\rquote m in the capital. I won\rquote t be back until the end of next week.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Ah\'85\rdblquote  she replied, nodding. So he\rquote ll be spending the week with his fiancee.\par
Once again, she looked down at the river. Ever since summer had started to approach, talk of the duke\rquote s upcoming wedding had been on everyone\rquote s lips. During her lunch break at the school, her colleagues had conversed about little else than their admiration and envy of Lady Claudine, who would soon be the next Duchess Herhardt. As always, Layla had kept a smile plastered on her face and agreed with everyone\rquote s words of praise. The wedding ceremony was sure to be magnificently grand and beautiful.\par
\ldblquote The river looks so pretty from here. It\rquote s like I\rquote m looking at stars flowing by,\rdblquote  she said. It occurred to her that she would probably remember this sight for a long time to come. She readily accepted this.\par
\ldblquote But Your Majesty,\rdblquote  he replied, snickering, \ldblquote isn\rquote t my queen afraid of the water?\rdblquote\par
She frowned at him. \ldblquote Don\rquote t tease me like that. I\rquote m not your queen.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote I seem to recall you saying it yourself,\rdblquote  he replied, shrugging. \ldblquote You said that if I was a gentleman, you were a queen.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote I said that back when you were a gentleman,\rdblquote  she replied, not avoiding his gaze.\par
She suddenly became aware of all the time that had passed since she had first met him. His frame was much stronger and sturdier, and he looked much more mature now, but he was just as attractive now as he had been then.\par
\par
\ldblquote You\rquote re not a gentleman at all now, so you can just call me Layla.\rdblquote  She quickly lowered her head, but there was no avoiding him.\par
He stepped in front of her and, putting his hand to her cheek, said, \ldblquote This summer, I\rquote ll teach you how to swim\rdblquote  He glanced down at the river, then looked at her again. \ldblquote That way, you can know what it feels like to flow among the stars.\rdblquote\par
She was taken aback by this unexpected promise. \ldblquote You\rquote re lying,\rdblquote  she found herself saying in a shaky voice. \ldblquote This summer, I won\rquote t be here anymore.\rdblquote\par
He narrowed his eyes.\par
\ldblquote I have to leave Arvis once you\rquote re married,\rdblquote  she continued. \ldblquote So we\rquote ll never be able to be here together again.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Yes\'85 you\rquote re right,\rdblquote  he reluctantly replied. \ldblquote See? You were lying,\rdblquote  she scoffed.\par
\ldblquote I\rquote ll still teach you to swim,\rdblquote  he said. \ldblquote The Schulter isn\rquote t the only river in the world.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Everything\rquote s so easy for you,\rdblquote  she observed.\par
\ldblquote There\rquote s no need to overcomplicate easy things,\rdblquote  he replied. \ldblquote Then\'85 is that how you think of me, too?\rdblquote  she impulsively asked.\par
He had wanted her, so he had taken her for himself and made her his mistress. He was going to marry someone else and live a life of luxury, without any concern about the fact that Layla would have to live the rest of her life in the shadows. His life would continue to be easy, ever so easy.\par
He said nothing in response, so she asked again, more earnestly, \ldblquote Do you think of me as just another easy thing? If not\'85 do you feel sorry for me at all?\rdblquote  She was done trying to keep up the act. Her feelings were too strong for her to pretend like she was cheerfully enamored of him. Even though she expected to\par
\par
get nothing out of asking him this, she continued. \ldblquote When you think about everything you\rquote ve done to me. Do you regret it? Even a little bit?\rdblquote\par
She was going to run away. She had not wavered in this resolution at all. No matter what happened, she was going to vanish from the duke and duchess\rquote s married life.\par
However, if he were to show even the slightest hint of sincere feelings for her, if she could detect a faint glimmer of anything besides lust, obsession, hatred, and sadism in his altitude towards her, then she knew that the revenge on him that she was pursuing would also leave a scar in her heart, and perhaps she would reconsider the whole thing.\par
They gazed at each other silently for a long time. Finally, he calmly replied, \ldblquote No. I don\rquote t regret anything.\rdblquote\par
His arrogant, unremorseful face still looked as handsome as ever. \ldblquote I didn\rquote t think so,\rdblquote  she replied, smiling faintly.\par
\ldblquote What about you?\rdblquote  he softly asked. His blue eyes looked as deep as the river.\par
\ldblquote I feel the same way,\rdblquote  she replied. Putting on the prettiest smile she could muster, she reached up to caress his cheek. \ldblquote I don\rquote t regret anything either.\rdblquote\par
It was the most sincere thing she could say to him.\par
