Hessen quietly approached the duke and said, \ldblquote Preparations for your departure are complete, Your Grace.\rdblquote\par
Matthias nodded and stood up. His assistant then walked over to him and started brushing his suit jacket with a clothes brush. While he was waiting for his assistant to finish, he looked out the window at the large garden down below. It was almost time for the roses to start blooming.\par
Layla, you came into my world just like a flower coming into bloom, he thought.\par
A faint smile crept onto his face.\par
It looked like Layla hadn\rquote t left for work yet. Perhaps he would be able to catch a brief, distant glimpse of her.\par
Before leaving his bedroom, he walked over to the birdcage. His canary was sitting on its perch, bobbing its head. He tapped gently on the one of the bars of the cage with his finger, and the bird chirped in response Just like every other day, his bird was happy in its cozy cage\par
After that short greeting, he left his bedroom. Just as it was occurring to him that he had forgotten to ask Layla if she had decided on a birthday present, he reached the mansion\rquote s front door.\par
\ldblquote Huh? Mr. Remmer?\rdblquote  his assistant said, stepping forward towards the gardener, who was standing in the driveway, gripping a dirty shovel.\par
Matthias, who had been about to get in the car, turned his head. \ldblquote What\rquote s the matter?\rdblquote\par
\par
Hessen, the butler, tried to intervene, but Bill kept staring straight at the duke. Bill had always been a little rough around the edges, but he had never displayed this level of blatant rudeness. The other staff members who knew him well exchanged concerned glances.\par
\ldblquote Hey, Bill.\rdblquote\par
Bill gulped. Trying to stay calm, he said, \ldblquote N-never mind\'85\rdblquote\par
The knuckles of the hand with which he was gripping the shovel were white. As he thought back to Layla down on her knees, begging him not to do anything to the duke, he was finally able to take a step back.\par
Gritting his teeth, he bowed subserviently to the man he wanted to kill. The duke nodded and got into the car. He looked just like the perfect gentleman Bill had always known, the Duke Herhardt that everyone admired.\par
After the car drove off, Hessen approached Bill with a stem expression on his face. \ldblquote Bill, this isn\rquote t like you. What on earth is going on?\rdblquote\par
Bill took a deep breath to stifle the urge he was feeling to swing the shovel at Hessen. As the butler, Hessen knew everything that went on in the House of Herhardt. There was no way he was unaware of what was going on between the duke and Layla. He had probably helped the duke get to her, thinking that it didn\rquote t matter what sorts of horrendous things he did, as long as they were for his master\'85\par
However, Bill once again mustered all his self-control to suppress his anger, and simply replied, \ldblquote It\rquote s nothing.\rdblquote\par
Everything felt meaningless to him now. His coworkers, who had been like family to him for decades; Arvis\rquote s garden, which he had grown old tending to; he was fed up with all of it.\par
\ldblquote I\'85 I just wanted to bid His Grace farewell. What\rquote s the matter with that?\rdblquote\par
\par
After giving this uncharacteristically wordy response, he hurried back to the garden. When he reached the flowerbed he had been working on when little Layla had first arrived in the mail coach, intense anger and despair surged up inside of him.\par
He flung the shovel to the ground and left the garden. Startled by his unusual behavior, his helpers grew concerned, but none of them dared ask him what was wrong.\par
When he reached the cottage\rquote s front yard, the mailman walked up to him, smiling. \ldblquote Oh, Mr. Remmer! You\rquote re here.\rdblquote\par
With trembling hands, Bill took the telegram that the mailman was holding out to him. It was a response to a telegram he had sent a few days earlier. Once the mailman left, he hurriedly opened the envelope and read the telegram. After a brief feeling of relief, his eyes grew stony with renewed determination.\par
He was going to protect Layla. All other thoughts faded away from his mind, leaving only that singular resolution. He was willing to lose everything else for the sake of protecting her. There was nothing in his life as precious or important to him as that girl.\par
