At the duke\rquote s direction, the chauffeur pulled the car over on the side of Platanus Road. The deep green leaves were rustling in the evening\par
breeze.\par
Matthias got out of the car and sauntered across the shadowy road towards his Layla, who was standing in the shade of a tree.\par
The two of them looked at each other for a while, saying nothing. The only sound was that of the leaves in the trees.\par
Glancing at his watch, Matthias finally broke the silence, asking, \ldblquote Have you made up your mind yet?\rdblquote\par
His departure had been delayed because of a lunch meeting. He couldn\rquote t miss the evening train, or he wouldn\rquote t make it to Ratse in time for the empress\rquote s birthday party.\par
\ldblquote About the birthday present you want, I mean,\rdblquote  he added.\par
\par
\ldblquote Oh, that,\rdblquote  she replied. As she stood there, gripping her bicycle\rquote s handlebars tightly, she looked even smaller and more youthful than usual. She gazed at him, saying nothing more.\par
He enjoyed watching her silently gather her thoughts. Even more, he enjoyed when she finally thought of something to say, and he got to hear her soft, pleasing voice.\par
He liked so much about her. He liked the way she thought and the way she spoke. He liked the shadows that her long eyelashes cast on her face. He liked her smooth, round cheeks, and her pretty, smiling lips. He liked the tough, defiant attitude she sometimes took with him, and the vibrant look in her eyes when she spoke her mind. He liked her rosy complexion and quick breathing, and the way she no longer trembled in fright when she saw him. He liked the way her smooth, petite body hung onto his, as if the two of them were the only people in the world. All these things gave him great pleasure.\par
\ldblquote I\rquote ve made up my mind,\rdblquote  she finally said, smiling. Only then did the sickly pallor leave her face, to be replaced by a healthy glow. \ldblquote Should I tell you?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Yes, tell me what it is.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote If I tell you, will you give it to me?\rdblquote  she asked in a pestering tone. The cold look in his eyes softened. \ldblquote Sure,\rdblquote  he replied, smiling. \ldblquote I will.\rdblquote\par
The smile quickly faded from his lips, but it left a trace of warmth behind.\par
She gazed at him with an expression as calm and peaceful as the spring breeze.\par
She knew that ha was too sat in his ways to immediately break down over the loss of a mere mistress. Most likely, he would experience some brief anger, and then continue on with his happy life and become Claudine\rquote s husband.\par
Since she knew that losing his mistress wouldn\rquote t have much of an effect in the short term, she prayed to God that his yearning for her would become a\par
\par
long-term illness.\par
To that end, she slowly opened her lips and said, \ldblquote I want you to love me.\rdblquote  Her hair fluttered in the cool breeze.\par
\ldblquote I would like it so much if you loved me,\rdblquote  she said, smiling brightly at him.\par
She hoped that this request would lodge itself deep inside him, and start to fester there, like a wound that wouldn\rquote t heal. She hoped that he would go along with his life, thinking that he was doing fine, until one day the wound would be too much for him, and he would finally collapse.\par
