the fourth street after the bell tower in the town square. Still not used to this town, she could easily get lost if she didn\rquote t pay careful attention. Fortunately, she was able to find her way home in one try today. Holding a large, paper bag full of groceries with both arms, she plodded up the stairs.\par
Uncle Bill\rquote s relative had helped them find an apartment on the second floor of a building not far from the town square. It was smaller than the cottage back at Arvis had been, but it was much cleaner. Of course, it was going to take Uncle Bill quite a while to get used to a home without a yard or garden.\par
