\ldblquote Of course I am. I\rquote ll have Dr. Ettman pay us a visit later and we can have him give us a full report on Matthias\rquote s condition. Stop your needless worrying\rdblquote  The\tab more\tab Elise\rquote s\tab face\tab darkened\tab with\tab concern,\tab the\tab more\tab assertive\par
Katharina\rquote s voice became.\par
Ultimately, Elise gave in and nodded at her mother-in-law, while internally wondering, Were Matthias\rquote s feelings for Lalsa deeper than I thought? Maybe so. Young love is often the most passionate. But this isn\rquote t just anyone; it\rquote s Matthias.\par
Matthias\rquote s aloof, unemotional demeanor had won him praise, as such qualities were highly valued in aristocratic society. Elise had always assumed that his behavior reflected his true personality, even though she had\par
\par
occasionally witnessed troubling signs that this wasn\rquote t the case. The two previous dukes, Matthias\rquote s father and grandfather, had not been particularly warm or friendly men at all. Perhaps Matthias was different from them in this respect.\par
However, he had been loo well-behaved as a child for this to cause her much concern. He was the House of Herhardt\rquote s masterpiece. There was no better way to describe him. She believed herself to have given birth to the living embodiment of the family\rquote s glory and prestige. This made the strange feeling of distance that she sensed from him easy enough for her to understand. Could that Matthias, her son, really be falling apart over a Jowly orphan girl?\par
She laughed at herself for her pathetic worries, thinking, I really mustn\rquote t let my imagination run wild like that.\par
