And yet, even while recognizing all of this, Matthias didn\rquote t regret a thing.\par
This perplexed him to no end.\par
If I could go back in time, would fact differently? Not a chance.\par
He could be put in the same situation a hundred times, and he would still make the same decisions each time. It was who he was. He wasn\rquote t a man of virtue and integrity like Dr. Ettman and his son. He pretended to be one while\par
\par
in the public eye, but when he was alone with Layla, even pretending to be virtuous was impossible for him.\par
I don\rquote t want her to become some other bastard\rquote s woman, even if it would make her happy. I\rquote d rather take her back for myself and make her miserable again. Either that or kill her. But this doctor wants to talk to me about the true source of my problems?\par
