Even as the enemy general was offering his congratulations, Matthias\rquote s mind thought of no-thing but Layla. Even if he had lost her forever, she would be forever his.\par
Layla was safe. He was sure of it. Of course, it was ridiculous for him to have such certainty. They were in the middle of a war. Anyone could die at any\par
\par
moment. No one could guarantee the safety of a fragile, defenseless woman living in a city that was being constantly bombarded by air raids.\par
However, it wasn\rquote t just any woman, it was Layla. His Layla. Thus, she was safe. It was a matter of faith for him. He needed no evidence to know it was true.\par
As the citizens started to come out from hiding and gather in the town square one by one, Matthias announced that the occupation forces would guarantee the safety of the citizens, as long as they didn\rquote t commit any hostile actions or put up pointless resistance.\par
