Sienne\rquote s last line of defense fell far more easily than expected. The fortress had been the last thread of hope for the Lovita army. Once the soldiers learned that it had been destroyed, they lost all their morale. After conducting a formal defensive battle, they retreated, giving up a key strategic point in the south. The decision to retreat was a wise one. If they had continued fighting to protect the already-crumbling front line, the capital\rquote s defenses would have been put at risk of collapse.\par
The Berg troops passed through the wide- open city gates and advanced towards the square. The cavalry led the way, followed by a procession of military vehicles carrying the general and other commanding officers.\par
\par
Sienne\rquote s mayor stood meekly at the gates, greeting the occupying army with a white flag. The city\rquote s safety had been guaranteed as long as they accepted the terms of the occupying army and surrendered unconditionally. This seemed to be their only option.\par
Matthias took in the unfamiliar city from his seat in the back of a military vehicle following behind the cavalry. All around there was rubble from buildings destroyed in the air raid, and yet Sienne seemed generally calm and peaceful. Perhaps this was an illusion created by the clear sunlight, and the fact that the color palette of Lovita\rquote s environment was much brighter than Berg\rquote s.\par
The army proceeded slowly through the city, as if they were appreciating the spoils of the war, before coming to a stop at the square.\par
The general got out of his vehicle and went up to the platform that had been erected in front of City Hall. The other commanding officers followed in a line behind him. Matthias walked with leisurely steps in this line, loosely holding his officers cap. When he reached the top step up to the platform, he gently placed the cap on his head. Dressed in his blue-gray uniform, he looked clean and elegant, not at all befitting the brutal nicknames he had been given since joining the war.\par
In a powerful voice, the general began his lengthy speech. It was a ritual he had repeated each time they had occupied an enemy city, but today he was showing much more passion than usual. He seemed quite excited about having reached the goal ahead of schedule, but Matthias wasn\rquote t especially happy about this. However, under such a beautiful autumn sky, he felt like he could accept anything.\par
His heart was full of a generosity and composure he had not felt previously. It had been like this since the moment he had first set foot in Sienne. And why shouldn\rquote t it be? This was where Layla was, after all.\par
\par
Standing with proper military posture, he looked down from the platform at the countless people gathered below. While his eyes looked fierce, as though he were a predator searching for prey, his lips held a tender smile, as though he were facing his love.\par
This contradictory expression seemed to be mildly disturbing the officers around him, but he didn\rquote t care. In fact, he seemed completely uninterested in how they were feeling. It was a strange atmosphere. He felt like he had sunken into an abyss, and yet also felt vaguely elevated.\par
After the long speech finally concluded, the crowd started to disperse from the square. Removing his officer\rquote s cap again and holding it in his hand, Matthias slowly descended from the platform. His slicked- back hair was as flawlessly neat as his uniform.\par
Having regained his health on the battlefield, he was back to his usual appearance. The fact that he had entered the war in a weakened state and then grown stronger and healthier day by day had greatly contributed to his notoriety.\par
Just as he had reached the bottom of the stairs, an aide came running up to him, shouting, \ldblquote Major, I found it!\rdblquote  He had a look on his face like that of a proud student who had just completed his homework.\par
