\ldblquote Oh, was I wrong about that? Did the baby come from sincere love? If you say so, I\rquote ll gladly accept the correction.\rdblquote\par
Rubbing the long stem of his water glass, he observed her expression. Blushing severely, she was back glaring at him. He chuckled at her reaction. \ldblquote So try again. If you put on such a great acting display in order to escape from me, shouldn\rquote t you put on an even better display in order to save your life?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote I won\rquote t fall for your tricks anymore,\rdblquote  she replied. \ldblquote This isn\rquote t a trick, Layla. It\rquote s a generous offer.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Until you let me go, I\rquote m not going to drink one drop of water. That fact will never change, no matter what.\rdblquote\par
\par
Occasionally she had wondered about him, thinking that perhaps he had grown. Now she felt ashamed to have even considered the possibility. He was the same as he had always been. He was tormenting her once again, just as cruelly and boldly, without showing the slightest sign of guilt or remorse.\par
\ldblquote I think it will have to change,\rdblquote  he remarked, narrowing his eyes. \ldblquote You see, Kyle Ettman is currently imprisoned, as punishment for his outburst. He seemed to have lost his reason over you.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote H-he\rquote s in jail? Kyle is? How could you?!\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote You can\rquote t blame me for that, Layla. This is the military. Rules are rules.\par
There\rquote s nothing I can do about it.\rdblquote  \ldblquote That\rquote s a lie! It\rquote s all because of you!\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote In any case, Kyle is in prison, and he\rquote s probably quite hungry by now. I\rquote m not the reason he was imprisoned, but I am the reason he\rquote s not being fed. It was my special request.\rdblquote  Sitting back in his chair, he crossed his legs and smiled. \ldblquote Until I see you eat, Kyle won\rquote t eat either. However much food I do see you eat, Kyle will get that much food as well. If you keep starving yourself like this, though, what can I do? Private Ettman will starve as well.\rdblquote\par
