When Matthias arrived back at the room, Layla was sitting by the window, looking exhausted. The sun had set, but she had not turned\par
on the light, so the room was dark.\par
After locking the door, he sauntered towards her and switched on the lamp. Just as he was about to draw the curtains, he was surprised to hear her speak first.\par
\ldblquote I ate,\rdblquote  she said. \ldblquote The brown-haired soldier brought me a sandwich and I ate it.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote So?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote So\'85 you should feed Kyle too,\rdblquote  she replied with a determined look on her face.\par
He stared back at her for a moment before snickering as he leaned against the window frame. He had expected her to make this request, but it still\par
\par
bothered him to hear it come out of her mouth.\par
\ldblquote I\rquote m not lying,\rdblquote  she continued. \ldblquote I really did eat. If you don\rquote t believe me, you can check for y-\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote I believe you,\rdblquote  he coldly said, cutting her off. \ldblquote But that\rquote s not a reason for me to let Kyle eat.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote But you promised!\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Did you forget, Layla? I told you very clearly that I would give Kyle as much food as I saw you eat with my own eyes.\rdblquote\par
He was growing even calmer as his words became colder. Her face went pale as she stared at him in disbelief. \ldblquote What do you expect to gain from being so cruel? What happened to the lofty pride of the noble Duke Herhardt?\rdblquote  She staggered up from her chair and walked in front of him. \ldblquote You abandoned your new bride and joined the war just so that you could chase after your mistress who fled you out of hate. What a pathetic man you\rquote ve become. I guess you\rquote ve thrown your pride away, huh?\rdblquote\par
She was still frightened of him, but right now her anger was overpowering her fear.\par
\ldblquote I don\rquote t know. Have I?\rdblquote  he casually replied, taking off his cap and setting it down on the table with a smile. Far from seeming angry at her, he seemed carefree and amused.\par
He\rquote s unhinged, she thought, suddenly remembering just how strange and unpredictable he was. She felt so much hatred for him, her teeth almost started to chatter.\par
\ldblquote What are you thinking?\rdblquote  she asked. \ldblquote What are you planning to do? Are you just going to keep tormenting me? Is that how you\rquote re planning to get revenge on me for deceiving you and running away? Do you think you have the right to do that?\rdblquote\par
\par
\ldblquote As the father of the baby you\rquote re carrying, surely I have at least that right, don\rquote t you think?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote How dare you say that?! I can\rquote t stand to hear you mention my baby at all!\rdblquote  She wrapped her arms around her belly and stepped away from him. \ldblquote You have nothing to do with me or my baby. So leave! Go back to the duchess and live your life with her!\rdblquote\par
She gritted her teeth to stop herself from breaking into tears.\par
Don\lquote t expect anything, she had been telling herself over and over again, ever since her improbable reunion with him. Now she feared that her expectancy was starting to grow again. If her heart were to break once more, she didn\rquote t think that she could stand it. However, he had always treated her horribly.\par
\ldblquote Think logically about this, Layla. How do you expect to survive as a single mother in the middle of a war?\rdblquote\par
He was now standing right in front of her. The smile was gone from his face.\par
\ldblquote My baby and I will do just fine on our own,\rdblquote  she replied. \ldblquote We can do anything, as long as you\rquote re not around. I find you much more detestable than the war!\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Layla Llewellyn.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Don\rquote t touch me! Don\rquote t lay a finger on my body! You\rquote re dirty!\rdblquote  Shuddering, she batted his hand away.\par
\ldblquote Dirty\'85?\rdblquote  he asked, chuckling.\par
Stepping back away from him until she was in the corner of the room, she replied, \ldblquote Yes, dirty!\rdblquote  Despite her fear, she was shouting vehemently. \ldblquote I hate you so much. You\rquote re dirty. You always were, and you always will be. There, is that a good enough response?\rdblquote\par
