A voice rang out in the hotel basement storage area, which had been turned into a makeshift jail cell. \ldblquote Kyle! Hey, Kyle!\rdblquote\par
Kyle had been sitting on the floor, leaning against the cold, stone wall, staring at his feet. He looked up indifferently at the sound of his name. Through the bars of the cell, he saw the familiar face of his friend, the army surgeon, and said, \ldblquote Lieutenant! What are you doing here\'85?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote What do you think I\rquote m doing here? I was worried about you. As soon as I heard what happened, I knew I had to come check up on you.\rdblquote  Sighing, the surgeon walked up to the bars and crouched down. Surveying the cell\rquote s interior, he noticed at tray of dinner sitting untouched in the corner. Just as he had heard, it appeared that Kyle was refusing to eat.\par
\ldblquote You should eat the meals they bring you, Kyle. Being stubborn like this won\rquote t get you anything. It\rquote ll just make you weak.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote What happened to the woman the duke\'85 I mean, Major Herhardt brought in? Has she been let go?\rdblquote  Kyle asked. None of the other soldiers would answer this question for him, and the concern in his voice was palpable.\par
\ldblquote Well\'85\rdblquote  the soldier replied, looking uncomfortable. After letting out a long sigh, he continued. \ldblquote She\rquote s still with the major. But I don\rquote t think he\rquote s doing anything bad to her. I think he\rquote s just holding her prisoner.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote That bastard\'85\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Kyle, get a hold of yourself. We\rquote re at war right now. No matter what personal feelings you might have about the major, he\rquote s your superior officer.\rdblquote\par
\par
The surgeon was surprised to see Kyle overcome by anger, when normally he was so well- behaved. \ldblquote Anyway, Kyle, you\rquote ve got to eat. How about you eat your food, regain your reason, and then apologize to the major? That\rquote s the only way you\rquote re getting out of here anytime soon.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote No. I\rquote m never apologizing to that guy.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Why are you acting like this, Kyle? It\rquote s not like you. Who is that woman, anyway? And what\rquote s her connection to the major?\rdblquote\par
Rumors had been spreading even more quickly now that both Major Herhardt and Kyle Ettman were behaving erratically.\par
The perfect gentleman Duke Herhardt, the son of his family\rquote s doctor, and the beautiful woman that had come between them\emdash it was a scandal that no one could resist talking about. The fact that none of the concerned parties were offering any details only made the gossipers more eager to speculate.\par
Kyle gulped and looked away, saying nothing. Major Herhardt hadn\rquote t answered any of the surgeon\rquote s questions, and it seemed that it would be no different with Kyle.\par
\ldblquote You should really eat. All right, Kyle?\rdblquote\par
Eventually, the surgeon stood up resignedly. The lights from the storage area hallway and the shadows of the cell\rquote s bars flickered over the cold food on the tray.\par
When the soldier took one last look over his shoulder before leaving, Kyle was still sitting in the exact same spot.\par
