Matthias gazed at Layla as she stood in place, staring blankly. As he watched her, his emotionless face gave way to a smile, which then faded. After this happened a few times, he walked towards her.\par
Firmly clutching the hem of her skirt, she stared straight at him as he approached. Suddenly, thoughts of Claudine had entered her mind. The more she tried to avoid thinking about her, the more clearly her memories presented themselves to her. She winced as she thought of the shame and humiliation the duke\rquote s fiancee had made her feel after she had found out about everything. It had made her feel miserable, especially since she hadn\rquote t been able to refute any of her accusations. She had thought that she had forgotten about all of that, but it seemed that she hadn\rquote t.\par
All throughout the late spring and summer, whenever she was sitting on the cold floor of the bathroom or huddled in a corner of the museum storage area, suffering from horrible morning sickness, she would think, Their wedding is fast approaching, and later, They must be married by now. Such thoughts came to her mind each time she had to hide the fact that she was pregnant.\par
As the fetus had grown inside of her, so had her sadness. Even after war suddenly broke out and turned the world upside down, her fear of the war still didn\rquote t completely eliminate the sadness. This was especially true when she had a sudden craving for some specific food, or when she saw a sweet newlywed couple with a baby. This would always make her think of the duke and\par
\par
duchess, whom she assumed had not only had a lavish wedding, but were likely expecting a baby of their own.\par
At such times, she would whisper to her belly, It\rquote s all right, Baby, it\rquote s all right. Mommy\rquote s going to love you double. So don \rquote t worry. This was how she had managed to endure things so far, and she wanted things to stay that way. There was no way she was going to allow herself to be taken in by the duke again and let the baby inside her live through the same pain and sorrow she had gone through.\par
Matthias stopped one step away from her. His face was cold and expressionless. She couldn\rquote t help but flinch, but she didn\rquote t avert her eyes.\par
\ldblquote Layla, how are you going to put up with the child of the dirty man that\rquote s standing before you?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote My baby has nothing to do with you!\rdblquote  she cried just as desperately as ever, even as she was growing extremely tired of his word games.\par
\ldblquote I guess you really love that baby, huh?\rdblquote  he asked with amusement.\par
Instead of saying anything in response, she answered him by putting her arms over her belly to cover it.\par
\ldblquote A woman who loves the baby of the man she hates\'85\rdblquote  After looking back and forth between her face and her belly a few times, he burst into dry laughter. His eyes remained frighteningly serious even as he laughed. \ldblquote How funny.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote You\rquote ve really lost it, haven\rquote t you?\rdblquote  she asked. \ldblquote Yep,\rdblquote  he replied, putting his hands to her face.\par
She tried to turn her head away from him, but his strength was too much for her.\par
\ldblquote I couldn\rquote t have made it here in my right mind,\rdblquote  he continued. She was taken aback by his calmness.\par
\par
\ldblquote Something I really like about you, Layla, is the way you always put your weaknesses on display for me.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote What are you talking about\'85?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote No matter how much you hate me, no matter how dirty or detestable you find me, in the end, you\rquote re always still mine.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote No. That\rquote s not true.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Yes it is. Because I will take the baby.\rdblquote\par
Because he was speaking in such a gentle voice, she wasn\rquote t sure she had heard him right at first. Now he started laughing as if he were suddenly overcome with joy.\par
\ldblquote Once the baby is born, I\rquote ll let you go. Don\rquote t worry, I won\rquote t kill you. You can run away wherever you want. You\rquote ll just have to leave the baby behind.\rdblquote\par
As the haze lifted from her mind and she grasped what he was saying, her resistance intensified. She tried pushing him, hitting him, and scratching him, but he wouldn\rquote t let her go.\par
\ldblquote Let go of me! Now! How dare you threaten to take my baby?! I\rquote ll never forgive you! Never!\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Calm down, Layla. You\rquote re going to disturb our beloved baby.\rdblquote\par
He lowered his hands from her cheeks and grasped her flailing arms. She kept trying to struggle, even after it became impossible to move her arms anymore.\par
Without exerting much strength, he was able to put his arms around her and lift her up. She was quite small even though she was pregnant, and she fit snugly in his arms as always.\par
He set the exhausted woman down on the bed and smiled warmly. It was the first sincere smile that had appeared on his face since she had disappeared in the spring. Even if she would never forgive him, he had found a way to hold\par
\par
on to her. The relief that this brought him allowed him to finally breathe freely.\par
Her lips twitched for a moment, but she didn\rquote t say anything. Instead, she just shed thick tears. He removed her cracked glasses from her face and set them down on the bedside table, then stooped over and kissed the moist edges of her eyes. Like an animal licking its wounds, he lapped up her tears. I guess I\rquote ve really lost it, he thought as he savored the briny taste. Well, that\rquote s line with me.\par
