\par
Matthias awoke very early, before the sun had risen. With his eyes still adjusted to the dark, he looked around the room. The first thing he\par
noticed was the empty spot next to him in the bed. It was odd\emdash -Layla had definitely cried herself to sleep right there, but now there was nothing but darkness in her place.\par
As soon as he realized this, he reflexively sat up. First he looked at the door, and saw that it was still securely locked. This brought him some relief. The door was the only way out of the room. Thus, she was still in the room, unless she had jumped out of the window\'85\par
At this unpleasant thought, he bolted out of bed and ran towards the windows. Both windows were shut and locked, but his uneasiness lingered. Just as his heart was starting to pound rapidly, he found Layla in an unexpected spot.\par
\par
He sighed at the sight before him. She was curled up on the sofa, fast asleep. When he saw the thin blanket she was using for warmth, he couldn\rquote t help but chuckle. He could almost hear her saying, \ldblquote Don\rquote t touch me. You\rquote re dirty.\rdblquote  She found his presence loathsome enough that she couldn\rquote t stand to lie next to him, and yet back in the spring she had smiled so beautifully at him. She had given herself to his embrace and whispered sweet nothings in his ear.\par
And yet, despite all those apparent signs of love, she had hated him all along.\par
As he quietly reflected on this thought, his face showed no expression. He had already been aware of this, he just hadn\rquote t fully accepted it till now.\par
Where was the line between sincerity and deceit with her?\par
Ever since she had first disappeared, he had been mulling over this question, and now he finally knew the answer. It had all been deceit with her. He had loved her, but she hadn\rquote t loved him back at all. Nonetheless, his memories of the show of love she had put on were still vivid, which only made him feel more miserable.\par
He gently closed his eyes for a moment, then opened them and carefully lifted her from the sofa and moved her over to the bed. She fidgeted a bit, but luckily did not wake up. Even in her pregnant state, she still felt remarkably light in his arms.\par
He placed her down on the bed very gently, then slowly pulled the covers over her body. Instead of lying down next to her, he pulled up a chair next to the bed and sat down in it.\par
Her face looked calm and innocent as she slept. It occurred to him that this was the way her face looked when she was interacting with anyone other than him. To everyone but him, she was a bright, strong, kind young lady. He was the only person in the world who was more accustomed to seeing her cry than\par
\par
smile. And yet even so, she was going to have his child. He felt silly for fixating on that fact, but he couldn\rquote t help it.\par
He didn\rquote t understand how she could hate him so much, and yet love his baby. Regardless the reason, though, it was his only remaining hope. He knew that because of her love for the baby, she wouldn\rquote t die or run away. Thus, if he could keep the baby near himself, she would become his again.\par
The baby would thus function as the perfect set of shackles, the perfect birdcage. That was all the baby was to him. He felt no particular emotions towards it. Other than its usefulness to him as a way to hold on to Layla, it was meaningless to him.\par
As he thought about it, he realized that there was one emotion he felt about the baby: regret. He bitterly regretted not impregnating Layla sooner. If he had, she never would have been able to run away in the first place.\par
As the anxiousness left his face, he started smiling like a child holding piece of candy. From the moment he joined the war, to the moment he finally entered Sienne, he had been wishing for Layla\rquote s safety. She had to remain safe from harm until he got to her, so that he could kill her himself. He didn\rquote t want to kill her out of hatred or resentment. Rather, it was out of love. Love had always been the reason he wanted to kill her.\par
He knew that her love for him had been a lie, and there was no way to forget that. Nonetheless, his love for her was as strong as ever. It felt like an unstoppable force inside him that threatened to devour the rest of his life. The only way to put an end to this overwhelming feeling, he thought, was to kill her with his own hands. Thus, until he could do so, she had to survive. It was imperative that she not die by any other cause.\par
With each passing day, his love for her had only grown stronger. And with that, his desire to kill her had grown in intensity as well. This desperate\par
\par
pattern had continued to this day. And yet, the moment he had laid eyes on her, standing in front of the beautiful sea, he had realized that he couldn\rquote t kill her. He wanted to kill her. He had to kill her. And yet, he couldn\rquote t kill her.\par
As he was reeling in the mixture of despair and joy that this realization had brought him, he had noticed her pregnant belly, and had known at once that it was his salvation.\par
