Layla stepped back from the closed door, looking exhausted as she panted and tried to catch her breath. Her attempt to break through the door by hammering at it with a metal candlestick had resulted in nothing but several unsightly dents. The door remained just as firmly locked as ever.\par
After staring at the door for a while longer, she turned away. She set the candlestick down, sat deep in a chair, and let out a long sigh. The fetus inside her, which had gone stiff as if it were frightened by the noise, started to move again.\par
\ldblquote Don\rquote t worry, nothing\rquote s wrong. It\rquote s all right,\rdblquote  she said, trying to comfort it. She started stroking her belly, and she could immediately feel the fetus moving towards the spot she was touching.\par
She was used to it by now, but the first time she had felt the fetus moving, she had been very surprised, almost scared. Unsure what to do, she had hesitated for a moment before tentatively touching her belly. The fetus had then made another quick movement, as if in response. It was then that she had finally felt like a mother.\par
A wondrous, joyful feeling had filled her heart in that moment. She was a little sad that she couldn\rquote t tell anyone about the feeling, but at least she could share it with the baby inside of her. She felt like the baby knew everything.\par
When Layla was in a good mood, she could feel the baby dancing joyously. When she felt depressed, the baby curled up stiffly. It was like there was a tiny\par
\par
version of herself inside of her. She loved her baby with all her heart. It was a love that had absolutely nothing to do with Matthias.\par
Once the fetus had calmed down again, Layla put her messy hair into a ponytail, and wiped the tears from her eyes before putting her glasses back on. No matter how desperate of a situation she was in, she was a mother. She was her baby\rquote s only family member and guardian.\par
She ate the lunch the now familiar soldier had left for her, and changed her clothes. Most of the things from her apartment had been moved to this room by now. It seemed that the duke really had no intention of letting her go.\par
Think calmly, she thought, trying to console herself as she looked around the room.\par
She had tried screaming for help, begging the soldiers to let her go, and now had even tried breaking down the door. None of these things had worked. Unless the duke had a change of heart, there was no way for her to escape.\par
She understood this rationally, and yet she didn\rquote t want to give up. She couldn\rquote t keep living like this forever. She had to protect the baby from the duke.\par
But how could she do that?\par
Just as her growing uneasiness was about to cause her to burst into tears, she heard the sound of the lock being unfastened on the other side of the door. She reflexively stood up and hurriedly lay down in bed. Feigning sleep, she closed her eyes and calmed her breathing. Meanwhile, she could hear the chains being lifted.\par
Lying curled up on her side, she clutched the edges of her pillow. A moment later, she heard the door open and then could sense someone walking across the room towards the bed.\par
From the sound of the footsteps alone she knew that the duke had returned.\par
