Layla focused on pretending to be asleep. She had started doing this out of a desire not to have to look at Matthias, but at some point, her fear had increased even more. She was now truly afraid of him.\par
Oddly enough, this new fear had made her realize that, though she had always feared Duke Herhardt to some extent, the version of him that she had known back at Arvis had not been completely cold and emotionless. This was clear now, when she compared her memories of him back then to the way he was now. He had changed. It seemed that she really had destroyed some part of his soul.\par
Does that mean that my wish was granted? she wondered, recalling that she had wished that his yearning for her would become a long-term illness. Rather than being completely forgotten by him, she had wanted to leave an emotional scar with him. However, this transformation wasn\rquote t what she had wanted.\par
Still feigning sleep, she bit her lip, feeling like she was about to burst into tears. She could hear the sound of the duke removing his overcoat and uniform jacket and placing them on the end of the bed. She then heard him walk a few steps, and then she felt the bed shake.\par
Stifling the urge to scream, she clutched the edges of her pillow tightly. He then lay down behind her back and slowly pulled her deep into his embrace.\par
Startled, she almost struggled, but managed to resist the urge to do so. Fortunately, he didn\rquote t seem to want to do anything more than this. Thus she\par
\par
knew it was better to endure it than struggle. If she provoked him, there was no telling what he might do.\par
She prayed internally for time to pass quickly, or else that she could fall asleep immediately. However, neither of her prayers were answered. Time passed slowly, and her senses only sharpened.\par
He kissed her hair, earlobes, forehead, and cheeks with a feather-light touch. Just as gently, his hands stroked her neck, shoulders, and waist. Through his chest, which was pressed against her back, she could feel the slow, steady rhythm of his heart beating. She felt frightened and sad.\par
His breathing then gradually slowed down, and his hands and lips stopped touching her. Once she was fairly sure he was asleep, she let out a silent sigh of relief. Even so, she lacked the courage to look behind her, so she just lay there in that position for a long while. His embrace felt as warm and cozy as ever, and this only made her feel sadder.\par
Once the sunlight started to redden in the late afternoon, she finally opened her eyes and looked at him. He was asleep, with a peaceful look on his face. The way his face looked now was just how she wanted to keep him in her memory, so that years from then she could describe him this way when she told her child about its father.\par
Of course, she had no intention of hurting the child by telling the full truth. Instead, she was going to say, \ldblquote Your father passed away while you were still in my belly. But he loved us so much. \rdblquote\par
Even though she planned to lie like this, she wanted to convey some modicum of truth as well. Perhaps she would describe his handsome smile and blue eyes, or his gentle voice. She wouldn\rquote t go as far as to bring up any actual memories of her time with him, but she would describe brief moments and impressions like that. However, that was for a later date. Not now.\par
