He untied the knots and freed her hands. Then he tied another knot around only one of her wrists, and tied the other end of the necktie to his own wrist. This time she just passively watched him, making no attempt to resist. She looked very tired and worn out. This was understandable, given all that she had been through today.\par
He turned off the lights, and then lay down next to her. Their hands, tied together as one, lay on the sheets, one atop the other.\par
\ldblquote Don\rquote t go,\rdblquote  he whispered as he slowly interlocked his fingers with her in the darkness. Even more quietly, he said, \ldblquote Stay by my side.\rdblquote\par
