Matthias placed what he had brought on the table. Layla could see plainly what it was\emdash a stack of books\emdash but she had no idea what his intention was in bringing it.\par
\ldblquote You can read these if you get bored,\rdblquote  he said in a slow and deliberate voice, as if he were educating an ignorant child. \ldblquote There are some mystery novels. You like those, right?\rdblquote\par
She said nothing in response.\par
\ldblquote There are some books about birds, too.\rdblquote\par
She sat staring dispassionately at the spines of the books, still saying nothing.\par
Desserts, flowers, books\emdash the things the duke kept bringing to the room didn\rquote t fit the situation at all. However, she lacked the energy to point this out. Besides, even if she were to point it out, she didn\rquote t think he would acknowledge the nature of the situation in the first place.\par
With a blanket wrapped around her belly, she took the top book from the stack and opened it. She wasn\rquote t planning to actually read it, but rather to use it as an excuse not to look at the duke.\par
\par
Sitting across the table from her, he looked at her with satisfaction. Her loosely braided hair ran down past her thin shoulder, touching her belly. He found the sight of this pregnant woman sitting reading a book in the sunlight beautiful and peaceful.\par
After skimming through the book\rquote s pages for a short while, she looked up at him sheepishly and asked, \ldblquote Will you let me go outside just for a bit? I won\rquote t run away, I promise.\par
He didn\rquote t like the sudden break in the perfect tranquility of the moment. \ldblquote I want to stop by my apartment. And I\rquote d like to pay a visit to Uncle Bill\rquote s-\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Layla,\rdblquote  he muttered, cutting her off. \ldblquote You no longer have a home or a family.\rdblquote  He stood up, walked towards her, and put his hand to her face. \ldblquote The only home you have now is with me. I\rquote m your only family. I\rquote m your everything now, Layla. All you need is me.\par
