\ldblquote It\rquote s a war zone outside. It\rquote s dangerous. You need to stay with me. I\rquote ll protect you.\rdblquote\par
She looked out the window in frustration before looking back at him. The bombings that the city was undergoing were no more frightening to her than the duke himself was.\par
\ldblquote You\rquote ve got to think of the baby,\rdblquote  he added.\par
She frowned at this advice. Whenever he talked about the baby in her belly, he always put on a warm, friendly face. He was acting like a father who sincerely loved his future child, while in fact the fetus was nothing to him but a means of satisfying his greed.\par
\ldblquote Please don\rquote t insult my baby like that. I hate it!\rdblquote  she said, wrapping the blanket tighter around herself in the vain hope that it would prevent the baby from hearing what the duke was saying.\par
\par
\ldblquote Insult your baby like that?\rdblquote  he asked, cocking his head in mock confusion. \ldblquote There seems to be some misunderstanding here, Layla. I sincerely love the\par
baby. Thanks to the baby, I don\rquote t have to kill you, and you and I can be happy together again.\rdblquote\par
He was speaking in a flat tone, with no trace of hostility. His matter-of-fact attitude caused her to lose the will to argue with him any further. She hid herself in silence again.\par
He bent over and kissed her round forehead before returning to his seat and gazing admiringly at her. Once the sun had set, he picked her up and moved her to the bed. It was then that he noticed her body temperature was a bit higher than normal.\par
\ldblquote You\rquote ve got a fever,\rdblquote  he said, frowning as he felt her forehead.\par
She shook her head and turned to lie on her side, facing away from him. \ldblquote I\rquote m going to sleep,\rdblquote  she muttered before tightly closing her eyes.\par
He sat on the edge of the bed gazing at her for a moment, and then placed the necktie on the bedside table, deciding not to tie it around her wrists. He then lay down behind her and wrapped his arms firmly around her chest.\par
While he lay there, holding his precious, sleeping Layla in his arms, he whispered many things to her. He told her about the home he was going to prepare for her in a place she liked. If none of the Herhardt family\rquote s mansions were to her liking, he would purchase another one, or have a new one built.\par
Perhaps he would buy a private island.\par
He could have a very tall tower built to confine her in, and the island would become their paradise. If she would just stay by his side like she was doing right now, he would give her his whole world.\par
\ldblquote I love you,\rdblquote  he softly whispered in her ear.\par
\par
For the time being, it was something he could only say to her while she slept, but one day he hoped to be able to say it while gazing into her beautiful green eyes. One day, if the prison bars of her fear vanished and yet she still didn\rquote t leave him, perhaps this would be possible.\par
Perhaps it wouldn\rquote t be too long until that day arrived. After all, she loved the baby. Once the baby was born, she might feel that it needed a father. He would be ready to step into that role. Perhaps then she would accept him, as it would be a way to make a family for her beloved child. He knew how important family was to her.\par
Feeling happy, he pulled her soft hair to his face and kissed it. He then kissed her slightly feverish forehead and cheeks, and then her bony shoulder blades.\par
I love you, he mouthed silently as he let a warm sigh escape his lips.\par
He buried his face in the nape of her neck. The scent of fresh roses emanating from her body was as sweet as ever. The fact that he was yearning for the woman who had deceived him made him feel silly, but happy. He loved feeling her in his arms. Not knowing what to do with his feelings, he just pulled her into a tighter embrace. Her soft body tossed and turned feebly.\par
He smiled with sadistic pleasure, even as he felt like crying.\par
