Layla opened her eyes and found herself immersed in the dim, reddish light of dusk. It was a peculiar feeling to wake up in this light. The previous days had\par
\par
already felt somewhat unreal, but this twilight made everything seem even more dreamlike.\par
After wiping the cold sweat from her forehead, she let out a feverish sigh and curled up her body. She stroked her belly as if to ask, Are you all right? The fetus moved slightly in response. This brought her relief. At the same time, however, she felt an intense, aching pain throughout her body. The mild fever and chills that had started a few days earlier had gradually grown in severity.\par
After losing Uncle Bill, she had managed to endure life alone in the ruined apartment. Since being abducted by the duke, however, she had felt like her mind and body were crumbling away like a cracked dam. She hated that this was happening, but her physical state wasn\rquote t cooperating with her will.\par
In fact, things had been difficult and frightening for her for quite a while. She only realized that now. She hadn\rquote t been able to sleep well in the days after Uncle Bill\rquote s funeral. When it was quiet in the apartment, she had found the silence unbearable. When the night breeze blew in noisily through the broken windows, she had feared that another air raid had begun. She had tried her hardest to persevere through all of this for the sake of the baby, but at many points it had been too much for her to bear.\par
She hated herself for only realizing this now that she was with Matthias. Even though she had been shamefully abducted and locked up, she had found it much easier to eat and sleep peacefully than she had when she was alone. It pained her deeply to acknowledge this.\par
The hardest thing of all, however, was the fact that the baby seemed to like Matthias. At some point it had stopped reacting with fright to the sound of his voice, or to the feel of his touch. Sometimes it even seemed to dance joyfully in reaction to his presence.\par
\par
Perhaps it wasn\rquote t that the baby liked him, but rather that it was just dazzled by the existence of another person besides its mother. It still lacked any family other than its mother, after all. This fact made her feel very sad and guilty.\par
She had discovered that she was pregnant with his child after running away and settling in Sienne. At first she had tried to ignore it, but she could only remain in denial for so long.\par
Once she accepted the reality of the situation, she had found it surprising how quickly she was able to love and accept the baby. Even though she knew what it would mean for her to bear an illegitimate child without the father\rquote s knowledge, she still loved it. Even though she knew that it would change her life forever, she still loved it. Even though she knew how sad and disappointed it would make Uncle Bill, she still loved it.\par
However, she hadn\rquote t had the courage to tell Uncle Bill about it. She had worried that he would think that her desire to keep the baby arose from a lingering attachment to the duke. This thought brought her endless shame. If she had known that this feeling of shame would stick with her, she might not have kept it from Uncle Bill after all.\par
After suddenly losing him, the most painful regret returned to her. Had the baby been lonely? Was that why it had taken a liking to such a cruel, heartless father? She hoped not. Any attachment to the duke would only bring it pain.\par
At some point, she drifted back to sleep. When she awoke again, she saw Matthias. He called to her: \ldblquote Layla\'85\rdblquote\par
It was dark outside, and he had switched on the lamp. He seemed to be saying something to her, but she couldn\rquote t make out the words. Somehow she felt both freezing cold and burning hot at once, and she was out of breath even though she was lying still.\par
He called to her again, more loudly this time: \ldblquote Layla\'85\rdblquote\par
\par
The baby became more active inside her. It seemed to like the sound of him calling her name.\par
What if it thinks its name is Layla?\par
This sudden concern seemed comical to her, so she tried to laugh, but only a feverish sigh came out of her mouth.\par
As he continued to call her name, the baby continued to dance excitedly inside her. However, she found it very difficult to overcome the drowsiness she was feeling, or the chills.\par
I miss Uncle Bill, she thought before sinking back into a deep sleep.\par
