It was a one-sided fight, with Kyle attacking and Matthias only defending. Having already served time in the makeshift prison in the hotel\rquote s basement, Kyle at this point didn\rquote t care if he would be court-martialed and executed for attacking his superior officer like this. As far as he was concerned, if he were able to kill that devil, it would be worth it.\par
However, no matter how much he screamed and swung his fists at Matthias, Matthias only calmly deflected his blows, while uttering the simple phrase, \ldblquote Save Layla.\rdblquote\par
Kyle couldn\rquote t believe it. The duke had tormented Layla endlessly, pushing her towards death\rquote s door himself, and now he dared to give such an order. And yet, Kyle didn\rquote t have the strength to refuse the order.\par
It was Layla, after all. Order or no order, he would have done anything in his power to save Layla\rquote s life. However, nothing he had tried so far had worked. Layla\rquote s condition had not improved at all. Occasionally she would regain consciousness for a moment, recognize Kyle, and talk to him as if she had been transported back to their childhood days, but that was it.\par
\ldblquote I\rquote m not talking about the baby, I\rquote m talking about Layla, Doctor,\rdblquote  Matthias said, shifting his gaze from Kyle back to the surgeon. \ldblquote I want you only to think of Layla. Come up with a way to make Layla better.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote But Major, the mother and the fetus are not separate. We have to consider their health together if we are to-\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Give her medicine,\rdblquote  Matthias firmly said.\par
A look of bewilderment passed over the faces of the others in the room.\par
The surgeon didn\rquote t know what to say.\par
\par
\ldblquote Give her medicine right now,\rdblquote  Matthias repeated. \ldblquote Lower her fever and bring her back to consciousness.\rdblquote\par
Kyle then intervened. \ldblquote She\rquote s already in her second trimester of pregnancy.\par
A strong medicine could cause her to miscarry.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote So?\rdblquote  Matthias replied, frowning slightly as he looked down at Layla, who was unconscious and struggling to breathe.\par
\ldblquote Go get the medicine, Ettman.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Are you proposing that we kill the baby?\rdblquote  \ldblquote I don\rquote t care what happens to the baby.\rdblquote  \ldblquote How can you say such a-\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Save Layla,\rdblquote  Matthias said in the same callous tone he had maintained throughout.\par
He was speaking from his heart. He knew that if the baby were to die, he would no longer have any way to make Layla stay with him. His last sliver of hope would slip away. This consideration had made him hesitate up to this point. However, now that it seemed likely that she would die if they didn\rquote t do something, he didn\rquote t care about forcing her to stay with him. He was willing to put up with the hell of being without her, as long as she survived. As far as he was concerned, there was nothing else to consider.\par
\ldblquote How can you so casually say that you want to kill your child? And without even thinking of how Layla would feel?!\rdblquote  Kyle shouted angrily, having run out of patience.\par
Riette, who had been sitting off in the corner, stood up. \ldblquote He\rquote s right, Matthias. You\rquote ve got to think about succession. We\rquote re in the middle of a war. If the baby that Miss Llewellyn is carrying is yours, you\rquote ve got to save it.\rdblquote  He was looking at Matthias with a serious expression on his face. \ldblquote If by some chance\par
\par
you end up dying on the battlefield, and if the baby turns out to be a boy, then he will be the one and only heir to the House of Herhardt.\rdblquote\par
Riette was offering the cold, calculated considerations typical of aristocratic society. Continuity in the line of succession was of paramount importance for prestigious aristocratic families, and the House of Herhardt was considered the most prestigious family in the entire Berg Empire.\par
\ldblquote Think rationally,\rdblquote  Riette said more forcefully.\par
Matthias glanced briefly at Kyle and Riette, who were standing in his way, and then turned to face the surgeon again. The heavy silence was broken by Matthias\rquote s calm voice saying, \ldblquote Go get the medicine. Save Layla.\rdblquote  It was as if these were the only words Matthias knew how to say.\par
