An ear-splitting scream filled the hotel room. Layla was screaming with such vehemence, it was hard to believe that only a moment earlier she had been lying lifeless on the bed.\par
\ldblquote Layla!\rdblquote  Kyle shouted, struggling as the surgeon and Riette held him back.\par
Everyone in the room looked highly distressed except for Matthias, who was staying amazingly calm as he held Layla down and poured the medicine down her throat.\par
\ldblquote It\rquote s all right. Everything will be better very soon,\rdblquote  he whispered as if he were comforting a child. After subduing her reckless struggling, he placed the\par
\par
bottle to her lips again.\par
However, she then started resisting even more fiercely, screaming like an animal being led to the slaughterhouse.\par
\ldblquote Stop! Go away! Don\rquote t do this!\rdblquote  \ldblquote Don\rquote t be stubborn, Layla.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote My baby! My family! How dare you kill my family?!\rdblquote\par
He furrowed his brow deeply as he watched her screaming in anger. \ldblquote You\rquote ve got to let go, or you\rquote ll die too.\rdblquote  The emotion soon faded from his face, and he forced her mouth open again.\par
Not knowing what else to do, she gnawed and scratched at his hands, and started sobbing. However, he remained unfazed.\par
\ldblquote S-save the baby,\rdblquote  she pleaded, grabbing his finger.\par
Her hand was as frail as a dry twig, but she was desperately clutching at him with all her strength. It would still have been easy for him to proceed, but her earnestness made him pause.\par
\ldblquote I-lied to you. It\rquote s our baby. Okay?\rdblquote  Her tears fell unceasingly, soaking her fever flushed face.\par
\ldblquote I know,\rdblquote  he replied without hesitation.\par
He had known the baby was his from the start, never doubting this for a moment. However, this knowledge did not in the slightest affect his decision to kill the baby in order to save Layla.\par
She stared at him uncomprehendingly.\par
The look of determination in his eyes did not waver.\par
\ldblquote But it\rquote s\'85 your baby,\rdblquote  she muttered. Is he going to kill the baby even though he knows it\rquote s his? How can he do that? \ldblquote It\rquote s really yours.\rdblquote\par
