\par
\ldblquote It\rquote ll probably look just like you.\rdblquote\par
\par
\par
\ldblquote You know, it likes you. Our baby likes you,\rdblquote  she said, growing more and more desperate as he remained silent.\par
He couldn\rquote t understand any of this. He had no idea why she was saying the things she was saying. Even if the baby resembled him, even if, as she perplexingly claimed, the baby liked him, none of that was important.\par
Previously, he had cherished the baby as a means to keep Layla by his side. Now, however, the baby was no more to him than a creature trying to take Layla away from him. He could not tolerate such a creature, even if it was his own offspring.\par
He practically climbed on top of Layla, putting the bottle to her lips again. \ldblquote No! Stop! Don\rquote t kill the baby! Let me die! If the baby is going to die, I want\par
to die too!\rdblquote  she screamed, struggling with all her might. \ldblquote If my baby is gone and I\rquote m completely alone in this world, I won\rquote t be able to go on living. So\'85 please.\rdblquote  She now lacked even the strength to keep her eyes open, but she clung to him and pleaded with all her heart.\par
As he looked down at her, his face sank. What about me? he thought. A scowl appeared on his face. I\rquote ll still be around, and yet she says that she\rquote ll be completely alone. Am I nothing to her? As he continued to stare at her, the bottle slipped out of his hand, shattering when it hit the floor. He snickered and said, \ldblquote If you want to save the baby, you have to survive.\rdblquote  He blinked slowly, and then looked straight into her eyes. \ldblquote If you give your life to save the baby, the baby will die as well. Because I will kill it.\rdblquote\par
He clutched her face. She stared at him with unfocused eyes, saying nothing.\par
\ldblquote Listen carefully, Layla. You need to live. If you want to save your baby, then you need to live. Do you understand?\rdblquote\par
\par
His hand started shaking as he tightened his grip on her face. She weakly nodded a few times before losing consciousness again.\par
He continued shaking her until Riette, unable to bear this nightmarish scene any longer, ran at him and dragged him out of the room.\par
Everyone who had witnessed the spectacle understood that if the woman died, he was going to kill his own child.\par
