\par
If I Can\rquote t Be Your Heaven.\par
\par
\par
Astrange sort of order developed between Matthias and Kyle. When Layla was conscious, Kyle would stay by her bedside; when she returned to her\par
deep sleep, Matthias would take Kyle\rquote s place. This routine had arisen naturally, without either of the men planning it.\par
Over the course of a few days, Layla\rquote s fever had gradually gone down. The surgeon was greatly relieved to discover that she didn\rquote t have pneumonia, which would have been the worse-case scenario and could have been fatal. The surgeon had good reason to worry that if the woman were to die, the major might have killed him.\par
\ldblquote What remains now is the patient\rquote s will and her strength,\rdblquote  he cautiously advised the major, who was holding the sleeping woman\rquote s hand. \ldblquote As much as possible, it\rquote s important to make her feel at ease, not frightened or anxious.\rdblquote  He knew that he was risking his life by saying this to the major, but it was essential advice for the sake of saving the woman\rquote s life.\par
Saying nothing in response, Matthias let go of her hand and stood up. Just then, Kyle entered the room with a meal for her.\par
\par
As the two rivals stood facing each other, the surgeon gulped nervously several times. He had heard all the rumors about Duke Herhardt and the Herhardt family doctor\rquote s son, as well as the woman the duke had abducted. Based on what he had observed over the past several days, these rumors seemed to be largely accurate. He couldn\rquote t openly acknowledge this, however, which made things quite awkward for him.\par
Luckily, the silent confrontation didn\rquote t last long. Matthias stepped away from the bedside, and Kyle took his place. Soon thereafter, Layla opened her eyes.\par
A bright smile spread across her face when she saw Kyle. \ldblquote Kyle\'85 Did you bring the geometry notes?\rdblquote  she muttered. She seemed to be confusing dreams and reality once again.\par
Kyle gladly played along. \ldblquote Of course I brought them. I don\rquote t think you\rquote d let me eat dinner with you if I hadn\rquote t.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Oh, come on. That\rquote s not true.\rdblquote  \ldblquote Let\rquote s eat, Layla.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote But Uncle Bill\rquote s not home yet.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote Oh, he\'85 said he\rquote s going to be a little late.\rdblquote\par
Kyle furtively wiped away the tears that were forming in his eyes, then smiled even more brightly.\par
Matthias watched the two of them from a distant corner of the room.\par
\ldblquote Oh, I see,\rdblquote  Layla said, smiling like an innocent young girl. Kyle then started carefully feeding her the lukewarm porridge he had brought. It was a cozy, peaceful scene.\par
After watching for a while, Matthias quietly turned and left the room. Dazzlingly bright sunlight streamed in through the windows in the hallway. A bitter smile appeared on his dry lips.\par
