Layla woke up and found herself in Matthias\rquote s embrace. The sun was shining brightly through the windows. It seemed to be morning.\par
As her mind became clear, hazy memories from the night started to come back to her.\par
She recalled grumbling in a half-asleep state, saying that she wanted to go outside, that it was stuffy inside and she wanted to get some fresh air. She seemed to recall Matthias listening to her with an uncharacteristically concerned, sympathetic look on his face. She wasn\rquote t sure if this had been real, or just a dream, however.\par
She shifted her gaze from the sky outside the open window to Matthias. He was sitting deep in a chair by the window, holding her in his arms. He was running his fingers up and down her spine with a touch as gentle as the sea breeze.\par
\ldblquote Layla,\rdblquote  he whispered, seeming to have realized that she was awake. He lowered his gaze from the distant sky to look at her and once again whispered in a sweet tone, \ldblquote Layla.\rdblquote  As always, he seemed to relish her name as it passed through his lips. \ldblquote The baby is safe. That\rquote s why I\rquote m happy right now.\rdblquote  As he spoke about the baby he had tried to kill, his voice was just as sweet as when he had called Layla\rquote s name.\par
\par
Feeling a little hopeful, she looked into his eyes. I guess he doesn\rquote t hate his own child after all. He only made that choice because his judgment got clouded in the heat of the moment. But he really-\par
\ldblquote I\rquote m happy, because I need the baby alive in order to maintain possession of you,\rdblquote  he said in an even gentler tone, crushing her hope. \ldblquote As happy as I am, though, I\rquote m also upset. I\rquote m upset that you, who hate me so much, love my baby. I can\rquote t stand that. I like the baby to the extent that it will function as shackles to keep you from escaping me. When I think of the baby as something that you love, however, I hate it.\rdblquote\par
She looked at him, bewildered. Perhaps it was because of the excessively bright sunlight, but his smiling face looked almost unreal.\par
Am I in the middle of a fever dream? she wondered. I hope so. No father should speak that way about his own child.\par
\ldblquote I know it shouldn\rquote t be this way, but I want to lock you up again\'85..I don\rquote t care if I have to hold the baby hostage and place you in a high tower somewhere. I\rquote m willing to do anything in order to have you for myself. And I won\rquote t regret a thing. I won\rquote t regret ruining your life, taking something precious away from you, or even bringing misfortune upon my own offspring. Even now, it pains me to know that I\rquote ve made you ill, but I\rquote m happy that I get to have you in my arms.\rdblquote\par
She held her breath. The baby, which had been moving energetically in response to the sound of its father\rquote s voice, calmed down as well.\par
\ldblquote This is just how I am, Layla. I will be a monster towards you like this forever. And one day this monster is going to make you die. I\rquote ll still love you, though, even if I kill you. So\'85\rdblquote  Trailing off with a sigh, he grabbed a handful of her golden hair, pressed it to his face, and slowly kissed it.\par
\par
Despite all his posturing, he knew deep down that he could never harm even a single strand of her hair. Even when he had resolved to find her and kill her, he had already known this. He had told himself that if he couldn\rquote t have her, he was going to put an end to his intense longing by ending her life. Even in that moment, however, he had known he was lying to himself. She was his ruler, his queen. There was no way he could kill her.\par
Seeing that she was trembling with fear, he slowly caressed her face to soothe her nerves. She could tear his heart to pieces with her bare hands, and he would sit back with a foolish smile on his face and let her. If his love for her was the poison that would kill her, then there was only one thing he could do for his queen.\par
\ldblquote Go, Layla.\rdblquote\par
Letting the handful of hair fall from his fingers like a golden wing, he put his hand to her cheek. The sight of her face still drove him wild with desire. This made him all the more certain that he needed to say this to her. If he were to let this moment pass, he might not ever be able to say it again.\par
\ldblquote You need to get well as fast as you can, and then leave me,\rdblquote  he said, forcing the painful words out of his mouth.\par
These words felt like he was issuing his own death sentence. Even as he uttered them, however, he maintained the smile on his face.\par
He loved everything about her.\par
He even loved seeing her when she was teary-eyed and distraught. Even though his obsession with her made him miserable, he loved the hell that he had created for himself. Even in this moment, he ardently longed to be able to live in that hell along with Layla and their child. That\rquote s what he was. A monster who had imprisoned Layla.\par
\par
However, he also knew that the woman he loved so much, the woman he desperately wanted to possess, was not just some woman. She was Layla, and was as beautifully free-spirited as a bird. She was the girl whose life he had read and read about while sitting alone in the cottage on that rainy day.\par
\ldblquote Layla\'85..If I can\rquote t be your heaven\'85 then I will let you go.\rdblquote\par
Even if he let her go, he had no idea how much longer his love for her would last. Probably for a long, long time. Perhaps it would continue to torment him for the rest of his life. Even so, he wouldn\rquote t blame her for it. He would continue to love her, and would endure all the pain that the love caused him. My beloved Layla, please\'85\par
\ldblquote So, go.\rdblquote  His voice was as gentle as a soft breeze. She stared at him in a daze.\par
\ldblquote Fly away from me and find your heaven.\rdblquote\par
Fly away before my love for you makes me kill you, he thought. Rather than saying this, however, he just kissed her forehead.\par
In that moment, Layla became certain that she was dreaming, and a smile spread across her face. The baby inside her once again started dancing like a flower petal swaying in the breeze.\par
It was a beautiful dream, even though it was a little sad.\par
