Layla\rquote s fever had gone down, but she couldn\rquote t stay awake with a clear mind for long. She still spent most of her time in a deep sleep.\par
Even though she seemed to have made it through the worst part of her illness, Kyle remained uneasy. He was still only a fledgling medical student, but he had years and years of experience watching his father work. With patients in conditions like Layla\rquote s, one couldn\rquote t be sure that they would recover simply because their fever had broken.\par
\ldblquote Uncle Bill\'85\rdblquote  she whispered, fidgeting slightly in her sleep.\par
She seemed to be dreaming about the past again. As long as she was sick, all that Kyle could do for her was stay by her side.\par
What could he do once she was fully recovered? This question made him even more anxious. There was no way he could simply leave her with the duke. However, he knew the duke wouldn\rquote t simply let her so.\par
\par
He considered deserting the military and taking Layla with him. When he considered how this extreme measure would play out, however, his despair only deepened. With the entire continent swept up in war, there was nowhere they could escape to. Besides, she was pregnant.\par
He tried saying the name that she had been calling out for: \ldblquote Uncle Bill\'85\rdblquote  His voice cracked with emotion as he said it.\par
If Bill were alive right now, what would he have wanted?he wondered. No matter how much he thought about it, he had no idea. One thing was certain, however. After escaping from Arvis with Layla and coming all the way here to Sienne, Bill would never have wanted her to fall back into the duke\rquote s clutches again.\par
So think, Kyle, think of a way to help her, he told himself, clutching his hair. Just then, the door opened, and he saw just the person he expected to see:\par
Matthias von Herhardt.\par
Kyle intentionally disrespected him by refraining from saying hello, but the duke didn\rquote t seem to mind. In fact, he barely seemed aware of Kyle\rquote s presence at all. From the moment he entered the room, his eyes remained fixed solely on Layla.\par
He approached the bed and started caressing her cheek. It made Kyle sick to see him looking at her and touching her with such intimacy, as though he thought she belonged to him.\par
Just as he was about to say something, the duke spoke first: \ldblquote We need to talk.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote What is it?\rdblquote  Kyle replied.\par
\ldblquote It\rquote s not something that we should discuss here,\rdblquote  the duke replied. Brushing Layla\rquote s hair back behind her ear, he stood up.\par
\ldblquote But we can\rquote t just leave Layla alone in\'85\rdblquote\par
\par
Before Kyle could finish voicing his objection, he saw a young military nurse step through the open doorway.\par
\ldblquote I think we can leave her without worry now, Ettman,\rdblquote  Matthias said to the stunned Kyle.\par
\ldblquote I have nothing to say to you, Major Herhardt,\rdblquote  Kyle said.\par
Matthias\rquote s face shifted the moment he heard Kyle address him by his military title. \ldblquote You seem to misunderstand me, Private Ettman. This is not a request. It\rquote s an order. A direct order from your superior officer.\rdblquote\par
Kyle realized too late that he had stepped into a trap.\par
Matthias turned towards the door before Kyle had the chance to make a reply. Kyle hesitated for a moment, and then followed him out.\par
They proceeded to have a surprisingly long conversation.\par
