Promises, Layla mouthed silently, as she looked again at the document Kyle had brought.\par
The document laid out the duke\rquote s guarantee that he would provide Layla and her child with the means for a comfortable life. It also specified that he was not doing this out of either sympathy or hostility, but simply out of a basic sense of responsibility. There was even a detailed clause stating that he would not intervene in her life any further, unless she so washed.\par
Furthermore, the document stated that Layla\rquote s child would be guaranteed the right to be legally considered the offspring of Duke Matthias von Herhardt, unless Layla would prefer to raise it without his name. Whichever option she preferred, he would respect her decision completely.\par
To this end, the document also specified obligations for Layla to fulfill. She and the child were to go to the Berg Empire, which was currently the safest location on the continent. If she wanted to move somewhere else after the war ended, he would respect her decision.\par
All other matters were left to her free choice. If she went to Ratse, the Herhardt family attorneys would ratify these promises.\par
Once again she stared at the document for a long while, hardly able to believe the duke had composed it when it contained such improbable words as choice, respect, and free.\par
She would need a while longer before she could fully grasp what was happening. She now realized that her conversation with the duke that morning\par
\par
had not been a dream after all.\par
Noticing the unfocused look in her eyes, Kyle said, \ldblquote I don\rquote t think we need to go right now. How about departing tomorrow?\rdblquote  He didn\rquote t want to rush her if she still wasn\rquote t fully recovered, but he couldn\rquote t help feeling antsy.\par
He had been completely taken aback by the things the duke had said to him in their conversation. He was letting Layla go. Kyle couldn\rquote t believe his ears. He still could barely believe it. Perhaps this was why he wanted to leave so urgently. Better to take care of everything before the duke changed his mind.\par
The duke had instructed Kyle that he was to help Layla relocate while he was away on his mission. Since her apartment had been destroyed in the air raids, he had prepared another place for her. She could stay there until she had recovered enough to be able to handle long-distance travel, at which point she would leave for Ratse. The duke had entrusted Kyle with the responsibility of supervising her during this process and making sure she remained safe.\par
Since she hadn\rquote t responded to his previous question, he asked, \ldblquote Are you all right, Layla?\rdblquote\par
She looked up at him but said nothing.\par
\ldblquote I understand,\rdblquote  he said. \ldblquote You must be shocked. I was shocked too. But Layla, this is really happening. There\rquote s no need to be hesitant or afraid.\rdblquote\par
He couldn\rquote t get himself to calm down. He had repeatedly told himself not to get too excited, but it was no use. He had gotten Layla back! This thought alone made his heart swell with joy. He felt like he had gone back in time, back to the summer of his nineteenth year, before everything had gone wrong.\par
Layla set the document down on the bedside table, and then carefully got out of bed. When Kyle rushed over to help her stand, she gently shook her head to refuse his help.\par
\par
As she tottered across the room, he followed a few steps behind her. Eventually she reached the door, and found that it wasn\rquote t locked. She couldn\rquote t believe her eyes. Her hands trembled as she reached out and touched the door. The chains and padlock were gone. All that remained were the dents and scratches she had created earlier while trying to escape. After a moment\rquote s hesitation, she tried the knob. The door opened easily without resistance.\par
The focus returned to her eyes as the reality of the moment set in. She was really leaving him. She was free.\par
