For the past few days, he had been entertaining a joyful fantasy. The war would suddenly end, and he and Layla would go to Ratse together. Once there, they would get married, and then they could raise the beautiful family that Layla had always wanted. He would gladly accept her first child as his own. Later on, they would have children together as well. In this way, they would live happily ever after\'85\par
\ldblquote I\rquote m not asking you to be with me again. I know you can\rquote t do that, Layla.\rdblquote\par
The fact that this fantasy could never be a reality only made it more beautiful to him, like a wonderful fairytale. His eyes grew solemn as he let go of that empty dream.\par
When she had called out to him in the middle of her fever dreams, he had known that it wasn\rquote t because she had lingering feelings of love for him. He had known at once that she longed for him not as a lover, but as a friend, and as a surrogate brother.\par
It was their childhood together at Arvis that she missed.\par
As much as he wanted to believe in the sweet fantasy he had constructed for their future, he had spent far too much time with Layla, and knew her far too well, to think it was possible. He knew that she would never be able to be with him when she had another man\rquote s child. No matter how willing he was to accept the child as his own, she would never accept him as its father.\par
\par
However, even if they could never be lovers, Layla was still his dear friend.\par
He couldn\rquote t stand the thought of her living a life of despair.\par
\ldblquote All I want is for you to be happy,\rdblquote  he said. \ldblquote And that man will never be able to make you or your child happy. Think about it, Layla. Think about what the duke has done to you. Your judgment is compromised right now because he\rquote s been tormenting you.\rdblquote  He was speaking quite forcefully.\par
She looked down at her feet. She knew that he was right. The duke had relentlessly tormented her, leaving emotional scars that would never heal, all for the sake of his twisted lust and obsession over her. He didn\rquote t love her. He wasn\rquote t capable of love.\par
Kyle walked up to her and, taking her by the hand, slowly but firmly walked towards the door of the room. As she allowed him to lead her, she felt like she was walking on clouds. He opened the door and they stepped out into the hallway, only to find Marquess Lindman there, leaning casually against the wall.\par
\ldblquote Are you really thinking of leaving, Miss Llewellyn?\rdblquote  he asked. His question made her wince.\par
