The team that had gone to deliver the message to the crown prince returned a day later than scheduled, in the late afternoon. At the staff meeting that followed their return, Matthias gave a report in which he described the situation in the rear and relayed the crown prince\rquote s thoughts on\par
the ongoing strategy.\par
He also reported that one of the soldiers, who had been severely injured in the shootout with the militia, had been escorted from the garrison directly to the military hospital in the rear, and that another soldier, whose injuries were comparatively light, had simply had his wounds dressed before returning to Sienne.\par
It was only after the staff meeting had concluded that the identity of the latter soldier was revealed to be Matthias von Herhardt himself. Despite his\par
\par
immaculate appearance, he went straight from the meeting to the military hospital.\par
When Riette heard about this, he rushed to the hospital, and found that Matthias\rquote s treatment had already been completed.\par
\ldblquote I hear you got injured. Are you all right?\rdblquote  Riette asked, looking with amazement at Matthias, who looked completely fine. He started to wonder if the news of Matthias\rquote s injury had been false.\par
Meanwhile, Matthias brushed past him, saying nothing. A faint smell of disinfectant wafted off of him.\par
\ldblquote Where are you hurt?\rdblquote  Riette asked. \ldblquote What happened? And what\rquote s going on with Layla Llewellyn? Huh? Say something. Come on.\rdblquote\par
Matthias said very little in response to Riette\rquote s persistent questioning, and then got up to leave. His face, posture, and demeanor looked just like the Duke Herhardt that Riette had always known.\par
\ldblquote Did you lose your hearing or something? Come on, speak to me,\rdblquote  Riette said, following stubbornly behind him.\par
Soon they were ascending the stairs of the hotel. Riette couldn\rquote t understand Matthias\rquote s behavior at all. After throwing away his whole life because of his wild desire for Layla Llewellyn, who was carrying his own child, he had given her up to the doctor\rquote s son.\par
Riette grew more and more irritated at the way his cousin was ignoring him, until they arrived at the door of Room 308. Matthias stared sullenly at the closed door.\par
Noticing the sudden shift in his cousin\rquote s demeanor, Riette couldn\rquote t bring himself to keep pestering him. There was a subtle mixture of resignation and anticipation on Matthias\rquote s face. Most people wouldn\rquote t have noticed this, but\par
\par
Riette knew his cousin well enough to sense it. You bastard, he thought about saying, before changing his mind and shutting his mouth.\par
Meanwhile, Matthias reached out and turned the doorknob. The door slowly opened to reveal the room full of afternoon sunlight. Everything was neatly arranged. No trace could be seen of the woman who had been imprisoned there.\par
Matthias stood there for a while with his hand on the doorknob, slowly surveying the room with a calm gaze. A slight grin appeared on his lips, making him look as serene as the afternoon sunlight.\par
He had let her go, and she had left. He calmly accepted this simple fact. The wild obsession that had been raging within him ever since he had lost Layla in the spring was gone.\par
It was a lonely, empty\rquote  feeling, but he could endure it. He didn\rquote t have the urge to escape or deny it. He knew he had to get used to it. After all, this was what his life was going to be like from now on.\par
He quietly stepped over the threshold and entered the room.\par
Following close behind him, Riette asked, \ldblquote Did you really do all those wild things for this? You hurt and humiliated Claudine, and then traveled into this warzone to capture and torment Layla, just for things to end up like this?\rdblquote\par
Paying no mind to his cousin\rquote s heated questions, Matthias casually removed his cap and overcoat.\par
\ldblquote If this is what you wanted, you could\rquote ve just\'85\rdblquote  Riette trailed off, forgetting the things he was about to shout. He stared in shocked silence at his cousin.\par
Matthias had taken off his uniform jacket, revealing a shirt completely soaked in blood. Riette couldn\rquote t believe his eyes. His cousin appeared to be\par
\par
severely injured, and yet not a hair on his head was out of place. It was a chilling sight.\par
While Riette stood at a loss for words, Matthias removed his blood-soaked shirt. The gauze wrapped around his waist was wet with blood.\par
\ldblquote Did you get shot?\rdblquote  Riette asked.\par
\ldblquote Just got nicked by a bullet or two,\rdblquote  Matthias flatly replied before lying down on the bed.\par
Muttering obscenities under his breath, Riette walked over to him. \ldblquote With injuries this bad, don\rquote t you think you should\rquote ve stayed at the hospital?\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote We\rquote re in a warzone.\rdblquote\par
\ldblquote So what? You think that means that bullets can\rquote t kill you?\rdblquote  Riette shouted, unable to control his emotions even though he knew that it would have been impossible during wartime to hospitalize a patient with wounds this severe or transfer him to the rear.\par
Leaning against the cushioned headboard, Matthias gazed calmly at his cousin.\par
\ldblquote You wild bastard,\rdblquote  Riette grumbled.\par
Matthias reacted with an amused grin. Despite his relaxed expression, however, he looked exhausted.\par
\ldblquote I\rquote d like to get some rest, Riette,\rdblquote  he said in a hoarse voice, blinking slowly.\par
Riette could understand his fatigue. After all, he had sent his woman away with another man, and was now pretending that nothing was wrong.\par
\ldblquote You wild, wild bastard,\rdblquote  Riette repeated. These were the only words he could find at the moment.\par
Matthias snickered, and then raised his arm over his face to block the sunlight.\par
\par
Riette departed, leaving the room in perfect silence. Matthias closed his eyes, and was transported in his mind back to the last night he and Layla had spent together.\par
After tossing and turning for a bit, she woke up and whispered, \ldblquote I\rquote m hot. \rdblquote  Having assumed that she was going to be looking for Bill Remmer or Kyle\par
Ettman again, Matthias was taken aback by what she said.\par
