Winter gave way to spring, and spring gave way to summer.\par
After an arduous war in which both sides suffered heavy casualties, the Northern Alliance finally emerged victorious. In many ways it was a pyrrhic victory\emdash the gains were small and the losses were large. However, in the eyes of history, the victory would stand as another glorious achievement brightening the legacy of the Berg Empire.\par
\ldblquote It\rquote s a dismal sort of glory, isn\rquote t it?\rdblquote  a noblewoman remarked, sighing deeply as she stood in line to greet the victorious soldiers returning to the empire. \ldblquote I suppose at the very least it\rquote s fortunate that the war ended before all of the empire\rquote s families had their lines of succession cut off.\rdblquote\par
